  "result": "I added `split(cents, parts)` to `shop/money.py`, and the full suite passes (10 tests, run with `python3 -m unittest discover`).\n\nIt gives each part `cents // parts`, then adds one cent to each of the first `cents % parts` parts. A `parts` value below 1 raises `ValueError`.\n\nThe new tests are in `tests/test_money.py`. They cover:\n- an even split;\n- remainder placement: `split(100, 3)` gives `[34, 33, 33]` and `split(101, 3)` gives `[34, 34, 33]`;\n- the parts summing back to the input;\n- `ValueError` for `parts` of 0 and -1.\n\nI didn't test negative `cents`. Python's `divmod` makes `split(-100, 3)` return `[-33, -33, -34]`, so the extra cent lands on the last parts there.",
